<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <SeoHead {title} {description} type="article" />
    </head>

    <body>
        <main>
            <SiteHeader />

            <!-- =================================================
                 HERO
                 ================================================= -->

            <header class="hero">
                <div class="breadcrumbs">
                    <a href="/#projects">Projects</a>
                    <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
                    <strong>AI Job Discovery & Outreach</strong>
                </div>

                <p class="eyebrow">Python · Google Apps Script · Workflow automation</p>

                <h1>
                    From job-board prototype to a{" "}
                    <span class="accent">multi-ATS job funnel.</span>
                </h1>

                <p class="hero-lead">
                    Version 1 was a Python and Gemini automation that pulled
                    vacancies from three job APIs and drafted outreach. Version
                    2 is a Google Apps Script collector that reads employers'
                    own job boards across nine ATS platforms, deduplicates
                    against my application history, screens conservatively and
                    prepares review batches, with a human making every decision.
                </p>

                <div class="funnel-graphic" aria-hidden="true">
                    <div class="funnel-sources">
                        {adapters.map((a, i) => (
                            <span class={`src fmt-${a.format.toLowerCase()}`} style={`--i:${i}`}>
                                {a.name}
                            </span>
                        ))}
                    </div>
                    <div class="funnel-lanes">
                        {adapters.map((_, i) => (
                            <span class="lane" style={`--i:${i}`}><i></i></span>
                        ))}
                    </div>
                    <div class="funnel-core">
                        <span>Normalise</span>
                        <span>Dedup</span>
                        <span>Screen</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="funnel-out">
                        <span>Review batch</span>
                        <small>human decides</small>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <SkillLinks
                    variant="hero"
                    skills={[
                        "google-apps-script",
                        "python",
                        "google-gemini",
                        "rest-api-integration",
                        "deduplication",
                        "workflow-automation",
                        "google-sheets-api",
                    ]}
                />

                <div class="hero-actions">
                    <a class="button button-primary" href="#adapters">Explore the ATS adapters ↓</a>
                    <a class="button button-secondary" href={githubUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">v1 source code ↗</a>
                    <a class="button button-secondary" href={dashboardUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">v1 Google Sheets output ↗</a>
                </div>
            </header>

            <section class="metrics" aria-label="Project metrics">
                {metrics.map((metric) => (
                    <article class="metric-card">
                        <strong>{metric.value}</strong>
                        <span>{metric.label}</span>
                    </article>
                ))}
            </section>

            <!-- =================================================
                 01 — WHERE IT STARTED (v1)
                 ================================================= -->

            <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="s-v1">
                <div class="section-heading">
                    <p class="eyebrow">01 — Where it started</p>
                    <h2 id="s-v1">v1: three job APIs, Gemini and a spreadsheet.</h2>
                    <p>
                        Built for a practical AI automation hiring assessment:
                        discover executive and administrative support vacancies
                        without LinkedIn, check their suitability and draft a
                        first message, keeping the final outreach decision
                        with a person.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="v1-grid">
                    <article class="card">
                        <span class="kicker">Discover</span>
                        <h3>Arbeitnow, Remotive, Adzuna</h3>
                        <p>
                            Each API returns a different shape, so normalisation
                            functions map them to one structure. Titles outside
                            the target roles and already-saved jobs are dropped
                            before any AI call.
                        </p>
                    </article>
                    <article class="card">
                        <span class="kicker">Validate</span>
                        <h3>Gemini, 20 jobs per batch</h3>
                        <p>
                            Three conditions (clearly remote, workable in
                            English, genuinely an assistant role) returned as
                            structured Booleans, confidence and a short reason.
                            Rules live in an editable prompt file.
                        </p>
                    </article>
                    <article class="card">
                        <span class="kicker">Draft</span>
                        <h3>Grounded outreach</h3>
                        <p>
                            Gemini writes a first-contact draft from the real
                            posting and a sender profile. The prompt forbids
                            inventing qualifications; nothing is sent
                            automatically.
                        </p>
                    </article>
                    <article class="card">
                        <span class="kicker">Run</span>
                        <h3>SQLite cache + Task Scheduler</h3>
                        <p>
                            A PowerShell launcher runs the workflow daily. The
                            Google Sheets dashboard (formatted with Apps Script)
                            holds the job details and drafts.
                        </p>
                    </article>
                </div>

                <div class="cache-story">
                    <div class="cache-copy">
                        <h3>The bug that taught the v2 lesson.</h3>
                        <p>
                            The validation cache keyed results on the job URL
                            plus a SHA-256 fingerprint of the job, prompt and
                            model. A repeated run only matched 33 of 69 known
                            jobs: the same Adzuna vacancy appeared under
                            different tracking parameters and URL paths. I
                            switched Adzuna to its numeric listing ID and
                            migrated the records; the final diagnostic matched
                            69 of 69, and a manual Task Scheduler run reused 70
                            cached candidates.
                        </p>
                        <p class="muted-note">
                            A diagnostic against already-evaluated jobs, not a
                            promise of a 100% hit rate on future runs.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="cache-meter" data-count-group>
                        <div class="meter-row">
                            <span>Initial repeat run</span>
                            <div class="meter"><i style="--w:47.8%"></i></div>
                            <strong data-count="33">33</strong><em>/ 69</em>
                        </div>
                        <div class="meter-row is-good">
                            <span>Final diagnostic</span>
                            <div class="meter"><i style="--w:100%"></i></div>
                            <strong data-count="69">69</strong><em>/ 69</em>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="verified-example">
                    <span class="kicker green">Verified v1 example</span>
                    <p>
                        A real Remote Office Assistant vacancy from Coalition
                        Technologies, found through Remotive, went through
                        every stage: discovered, evaluated, draft generated and
                        saved to Sheets. No fictional vacancies were added to
                        the demonstration dashboard.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- =================================================
                 02 — WHY REBUILD
                 ================================================= -->

            <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="s-why">
                <div class="section-heading">
                    <p class="eyebrow">02 — Why rebuild it</p>
                    <h2 id="s-why">Aggregators were the wrong source of truth.</h2>
                    <p>
                        For my own search (operations, marketplace and
                        e-commerce roles) the employers I care about publish
                        on their own ATS job boards. Aggregator feeds gave
                        shortened descriptions and partial coverage, and
                        title-based dedup could silently drop a different job
                        with the same name.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="why-grid">
                    <article class="card why-card">
                        <span class="why-from">v1 assumption</span>
                        <p>Three aggregators are enough coverage.</p>
                        <span class="why-to">v2 rule</span>
                        <p>Read each employer's own public board, one verified source at a time.</p>
                    </article>
                    <article class="card why-card">
                        <span class="why-from">v1 assumption</span>
                        <p>Same company + same title = duplicate.</p>
                        <span class="why-to">v2 rule</span>
                        <p>Identity is the provider's posting ID. Title similarity is a warning for a human.</p>
                    </article>
                    <article class="card why-card">
                        <span class="why-from">v1 assumption</span>
                        <p>An AI call decides fit on every run.</p>
                        <span class="why-to">v2 rule</span>
                        <p>Deterministic rules first, a manual review batch for the rest, cached until the job changes.</p>
                    </article>
                    <article class="card why-card">
                        <span class="why-from">v1 assumption</span>
                        <p>An empty response means no jobs.</p>
                        <span class="why-to">v2 rule</span>
                        <p>403, 429, a malformed page or a missing page is PARTIAL or BLOCKED, never zero.</p>
                    </article>
                </div>

                <div class="registry">
                    <div class="registry-copy">
                        <h3>Starting point: a 389-employer research registry.</h3>
                        <p>
                            The reference registry tracked 389 employers. Only
                            40 had an identified ATS; 349 were still unknown and
                            none had a tested public endpoint. That is why v2
                            needed source onboarding and verification, not just
                            more adapters.
